What Archify Studio adds on top of Archify
================================================================================

Original work in this repository (backend/, frontend/, Dockerfile,
docker-compose.yml, and this NOTICE):

  - A simplified JSON authoring format and a translator (backend/simple.mjs)
    that infers Archify's verbose layout (lane/col/pos/mainPath/viewBox) per
    diagram type.
  - A Fastify HTTP backend that drives the Archify engine and exposes render,
    export, and CRUD endpoints, with an LRU render cache.
  - A Vite + React web editor: a JSON text pane with a live preview of the
    HTML that the Archify engine generates.
  - Local persistence via SQLite (better-sqlite3), self-contained.
  - Containerized single-instance deployment (Dockerfile + docker-compose.yml).

Archify Studio does not modify the engine; it consumes it as a dependency.
